course: dictionary
lesson: 14546
title: Peruvian
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Peruvian is an adjective. It describes something that comes from Peru, a country in South America, or that belongs to Peru. «The Peruvian market sold colourful woven scarves.» Peruvian tells us which market: the one in Peru.
explain: A Peruvian is a noun: a person from Peru. You can add an s to make Peruvians. «My friend's grandmother is a Peruvian who moved to London.» We write Peruvian with a capital P because it is the name of a country.
explain: Context helps you check the meaning. If a text talks about the Andes, Machu Picchu or Quechua, it is probably about Peru. Try the swap: put «from Peru» in place of Peruvian. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Peruvian means from or belonging to Peru, a country in South America.
fact: A Peruvian is a person from Peru. The plural is Peruvians.
fact: Peruvians speak Spanish, and many also speak Quechua or Aymara.
fact: Machu Picchu, the Andes mountains and the Amazon rainforest are all in Peru.
fact: Potatoes were first grown in Peru, and quinoa is a Peruvian food.
exercise: «The Peruvian market sold colourful woven scarves.» What does Peruvian mean here? | A kind of scarf | Very colourful | *From Peru | From Spain
exercise: «My friend's grandmother is a Peruvian who moved to London.» What is a Peruvian? | A kind of potato | A city in London | *A person from Peru | A tall mountain
exercise: Find the word in «Peruvians speak Spanish, and many speak Quechua.» that means people from Peru. | Spanish | speak | Quechua | *Peruvians
test: Which country is Machu Picchu in? | Brazil | Spain | Chile | *Peru
test: Which word in «Peruvian food includes potatoes and quinoa» tells you where the food comes from? | includes | *Peruvian | potatoes | Food
exam: What does Peruvian tell us about the guide in «A Peruvian guide took us up the Andes»? | That the guide is a mountain | That the guide is very tall | *That the guide comes from Peru | Where the guide is going next
